# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""The icon set.

Sourced from Freepik and normalised here rather than used as downloaded.
Each one arrived with its own viewBox, its own units and its own idea of how
much of the box the artwork should fill — put side by side untouched they do
not read as a set. Every icon below has been:

  * measured for its real ink extent and scaled so all of them cover the same
    48% of a 40x40 box
  * centred on that box
  * switched to currentColor so it takes the site palette
  * (for the stroked ones) had stroke-width rewritten so that after scaling it
    lands on the same 1.6 as everything else

WHAT NORMALISING CANNOT FIX: five of these are solid fills and two are
outlines. That is a difference in construction, not in size or colour, and it
is visible when they sit in a row. The two outlines are IDENTITY and
D_PALETTE. Replacing those two with solid versions from the same source would
make the set coherent.

The previous hand-drawn set is kept in _source/icons-drawn.py. Nothing imports
it — it is history, not a module to switch back to.
"""

